IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `htta-donation`

-- Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask, with the seat and the situation
-- as parameters.
--
-- SEATS (`my role`, "Which of these describes you"): the donor, living or after death, and the next of kin, the two
-- seats the baseline was written from; and the parent or guardian of a child who may give tissue or blood, whose one
-- question the baseline also asks (ss 11-19). Every exported question takes `my role` first. A question about another
-- role answers `does not arise for you` without reading any other input, so the form never asks those inputs. The
-- designated officer, the coroner, the Minister and the medical practitioners are never a seat: what they decide or are
-- satisfied of is asked as a fact, as in the baseline.
--
-- SITUATIONS (graffiti design D8). Within a role, a question that arises only in a situation takes that situation's
-- fact straight after `my role`, and when it does not hold answers `does not arise for you` without reading anything
-- else. All are BOOLEAN, and FALSE gives `does not arise for you`:
--   - for the donor, `I have signed a consent to give tissue or blood while I am alive`: whether the tissue may be
--     removed now under it (ss 8(2), 9(2), 15, 16, 20);
--   - for the next of kin, `the person is kept breathing by artificial means`: whether the s 24(2) brain-death
--     declarations have been made;
--   - for the next of kin, `I made my consent known while the person was unconscious, before death`: whether the
--     designated officer may act on that consent (s 22(4)).
-- No question that arises in every situation of its role takes one.
--
-- Each question calls the baseline function of the same subject in htta-donation.l4 and restates no rule; where its
-- situation holds its answer is the baseline export's, carried in the answer types below. The next of kin's questions
-- about the person who died call the donor's functions with the person's record. No exported question takes a DEONTIC
-- or EVENT input.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I may give tissue or blood, or want to know what happens to my body after I die`
    `I am next of kin of a person who has died, or may soon die`
    `I am the parent or guardian of a child under 18 who may give tissue or blood`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

-- ss 22, 23, carried: the baseline's four answers, worded so the donor and the next of kin can both read them, and
-- `does not arise for you`.
DECLARE `Whose consent answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the person's own wish or consent, which no one's objection overrides (s 22(2)(a))`
    `the consent of the senior available next of kin (s 22(2)(b))`
    `no one's yet: the coroner must first consent (s 23)`
    `no one's: there is no authority to remove the tissue`

-- s 29A(3): "imprisonment for 12 months or a fine of $12 000".
DECLARE `Penalty answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `imprisonment or a fine, at most` HAS `the months` IS A NUMBER
                                          `the dollars` IS A NUMBER

§§ `Carrying the baseline's answers`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

-- Every value is listed, with no OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31).
GIVEN `the answer` IS A `Whose consent governs`
GIVETH A `Whose consent answer`
`whose consent, carried` `the answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `my own wish or consent, which no one else's objection overrides (s 22(2)(a))` THEN `the person's own wish or consent, which no one's objection overrides (s 22(2)(a))`
    WHEN `my senior available next of kin's consent (s 22(2)(b))` THEN `the consent of the senior available next of kin (s 22(2)(b))`
    WHEN `no one's yet: the coroner must first consent (s 23)` THEN `no one's yet: the coroner must first consent (s 23)`
    WHEN `no one's: there is no authority to remove my tissue` THEN `no one's: there is no authority to remove the tissue`

GIVEN `the penalty` IS A Penalty
GIVETH A `Penalty answer`
`the penalty, carried` `the penalty` MEANS
    `imprisonment or a fine, at most` (`the penalty`'s `months of imprisonment`) (`the penalty`'s `fine in dollars`)

§§ `For the donor, living or after death (the baseline's first seat)`

-- Each question calls the baseline's function of the same subject (htta-donation.l4) and restates no rule: for this
-- role, and where its situation holds, its answer is the baseline's, carried in the answer types above.

§§§ `ss 22, 23, 24 -- after I die`

@export Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after I die (Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) ss 22, 23)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A Deceased @desc The facts of your death, your recorded wishes and your family
GIVETH A `Whose consent answer`
`Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after I die` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I may give tissue or blood, or want to know what happens to my body after I die` THEN `whose consent, carried` (`Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after death` `me`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can my next of kin's objection stop removal of tissue from my body after I die (Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) s 22(2), (5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my relative` IS A Relative @desc The relative who objects
      `me` IS A Deceased @desc The facts of your death, your recorded wishes and your family
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can my next of kin's objection stop my tissue being taken after I die` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I may give tissue or blood, or want to know what happens to my body after I die` THEN `yes if` (`Does my relative's objection stop the removal` `my relative` `me`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Have the brain-death declarations section 24(2) requires been made about me (Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) s 24(2), (3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the declarers` IS A LIST OF Practitioner @desc The medical practitioners who examined you and what they declared
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Have the brain-death declarations been made about me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I may give tissue or blood, or want to know what happens to my body after I die` THEN `yes if` (`Have the section 24(2) declarations been made` `the declarers`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May tissue be removed from my body after I die (Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) ss 22, 23, 24(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A Deceased @desc The facts of your death, your recorded wishes, your family and any brain-death declarations
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May tissue be removed from my body after I die` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I may give tissue or blood, or want to know what happens to my body after I die` THEN `yes if` (`May my tissue be removed after my death` `me`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May this person remove this tissue from my body under the authority (Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) ss 24(1), (1A), 24A(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the remover` IS A Remover @desc Who would remove the tissue
      `the tissue` IS A `Tissue after death` @desc The kind of tissue
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May this person remove this tissue from my body` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I may give tissue or blood, or want to know what happens to my body after I die` THEN `yes if` (`May this person remove my tissue` `the remover` `the tissue`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 8, 9, 15, 16, 18, 20 -- giving tissue or blood while I am alive`

@export May I consent to giving this tissue for this purpose while I am alive (Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) ss 8, 9, 18)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the consent` IS A `My consent` @desc Your age and how you consent
      `the tissue` IS A `Living tissue` @desc The tissue you would give
      `the purpose` IS A Purpose @desc What the tissue is for
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I consent to giving this tissue while I am alive, for this purpose` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I may give tissue or blood, or want to know what happens to my body after I die` THEN `yes if` (`May I consent to giving this tissue while I am alive` `the consent` `the tissue` `the purpose`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May my tissue be removed now under the consent I gave while alive (Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) ss 8(2), 9(2), 15, 16, 20)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have signed a consent to give tissue or blood while I am alive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have signed a consent under Part 2 to the removal of tissue or blood from your body while you are alive
      `the tissue` IS A `Living tissue` @desc The tissue you consented to give
      `hours since I signed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours have passed since you signed the consent
      `I revoked my consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have revoked the consent, orally or in writing
      `the remover gave me the medical advice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the practitioner who would remove it is the one who advised you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May my tissue be removed now under the consent I signed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I may give tissue or blood, or want to know what happens to my body after I die` THEN
        IF `I have signed a consent to give tissue or blood while I am alive`
        THEN `yes if` (`May my tissue be removed now under my consent` `the tissue` `hours since I signed` `I revoked my consent` `the remover gave me the medical advice`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 29, 29A -- selling tissue`

@export Is my agreement to sell my tissue or my body void, and an offence (Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) ss 29, 29A(2)-(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the deal` IS A Deal @desc What you agreed to, and for what
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my agreement to sell my tissue void and an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I may give tissue or blood, or want to know what happens to my body after I die` THEN `yes if` (`Is my agreement void and an offence` `the deal`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be punished for entering a void agreement to sell tissue (Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) s 29A(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Penalty answer`
`What is the most I can be punished for a void agreement to sell tissue` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I may give tissue or blood, or want to know what happens to my body after I die` THEN `the penalty, carried` (`What is the most I can be punished for trading in tissue`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 34 -- my identity as a donor`

@export May someone make my identity as a donor or recipient publicly known (Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) s 34)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the reason` IS A `Reason for disclosure` @desc Why the information is disclosed
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May my identity as a donor be made public` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I may give tissue or blood, or want to know what happens to my body after I die` THEN `yes if` (`May my identity as a donor be disclosed` `the reason`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the next of kin (the baseline's second seat; ss 3(1), 22, 23, 24(2))`

-- The baseline's next-of-kin questions, and the after-death questions asked of the person who died, called from the
-- relative's side: the relative's own record is `me`, the person's is `the person`.

§§§ `s 3(1) -- am I next of kin, and am I the senior`

@export Am I next of kin of the person, under the Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) s 3(1)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A Relative @desc Who you are to the person, your age, whether you are available, and whether you consent or object
      `the person` IS A Deceased @desc The person whose tissue is in question, the facts of their death and their family
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I next of kin of the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am next of kin of a person who has died, or may soon die` THEN `yes if` (`Am I next of kin` `me` `the person`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I the senior available next of kin of the person (Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) s 3(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A Relative @desc Who you are to the person, your age, whether you are available, and whether you consent or object
      `the person` IS A Deceased @desc The person whose tissue is in question, the facts of their death and their family
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I the senior available next of kin of the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am next of kin of a person who has died, or may soon die` THEN `yes if` (`Am I the senior available next of kin` `me` `the person`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 22, 23, 24(2) -- the person's tissue after death`

@export Does my objection, as next of kin, stop removal of tissue from the person's body after death (Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) s 22(2), (5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A Relative @desc Who you are to the person, your age, whether you are available, and whether you consent or object
      `the person` IS A Deceased @desc The person whose tissue is in question, the facts of their death and their family
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does my objection stop the person's tissue being taken` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am next of kin of a person who has died, or may soon die` THEN `yes if` (`Does my relative's objection stop the removal` `me` `the person`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Whose consent governs donation of the person's tissue after death (Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) ss 22, 23)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the person` IS A Deceased @desc The person whose tissue is in question, the facts of their death and their family
GIVETH A `Whose consent answer`
`Whose consent governs donation of the person's tissue` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am next of kin of a person who has died, or may soon die` THEN `whose consent, carried` (`Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after death` `the person`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May tissue be removed from the person's body after death (Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) ss 22, 23, 24(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the person` IS A Deceased @desc The person whose tissue is in question, the facts of their death and their family
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May tissue be removed from the person's body` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am next of kin of a person who has died, or may soon die` THEN `yes if` (`May my tissue be removed after my death` `the person`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export The person is kept breathing by machine: have the brain-death declarations section 24(2) requires been made (Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) s 24(2), (3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the person is kept breathing by artificial means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person's respiration and the circulation of their blood are being maintained by artificial means (s 24(2))
      `the declarers` IS A LIST OF Practitioner @desc The medical practitioners who examined the person and what they declared
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Have the brain-death declarations been made about the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am next of kin of a person who has died, or may soon die` THEN
        IF `the person is kept breathing by artificial means`
        THEN `yes if` (`Have the section 24(2) declarations been made` `the declarers`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May the designated officer act on the consent I gave as senior next of kin while the person was unconscious (Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) s 22(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I made my consent known while the person was unconscious, before death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, as the senior available next of kin, you told the designated officer you consent while the person was unconscious and had not yet died (s 22(4))
      `me` IS A Relative @desc Who you are to the person, your age, whether you are available, and whether you consent or object
      `the person` IS A Deceased @desc The person whose tissue is in question, the facts of their death and their family
      `the person recovered consciousness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person recovered consciousness after you gave your consent
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the officer act on the consent I gave while the person was unconscious` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am next of kin of a person who has died, or may soon die` THEN
        IF `I made my consent known while the person was unconscious, before death`
        THEN `yes if` (`May my consent given during unconsciousness be acted on` `me` `the person` `the person recovered consciousness`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the parent or guardian of a child donor (the baseline's child-donation question; ss 11-14, 17, 19)`

-- s 11 onwards address the parent of a child; the baseline asks the question from the parent's seat.

§§§ `ss 11-14, 17, 19 -- tissue or blood from my child`

@export May tissue or blood be taken from my child, who is under 18, for another person (Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) ss 11-14, 17, 19)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the donation` IS A `My child's donation` @desc The tissue, who consents and what your child understands and agrees to
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May tissue or blood be taken from my child for another person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the parent or guardian of a child under 18 who may give tissue or blood` THEN `yes if` (`May tissue be taken from my child` `the donation`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
